              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, Congress enacted \u00a7\u202f7609 to give the public privacy rights to notice and an opportunity to quash third\u2011party IRS summonses, and carefully limited the exceptions."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ed40ef933c84dc7711bb4329fc16f9eb5d364590e17b6842b44f42a142a6a6d0",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ed40ef933c84-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 12,
                "start": 12
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, clause (i) concerns assessments or judgments against a taxpayer, while clause (ii) concerns the liability of a transferee or fiduciary; the notice exception distinguishes between them."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ed40ef933c84dc7711bb4329fc16f9eb5d364590e17b6842b44f42a142a6a6d0",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ed40ef933c84-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 13,
                "start": 13
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, Congress enacted \u00a7\u202f7609 in response to earlier decisions that gave a broad construction to the IRS\u2019s summons power, reflecting privacy concerns."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioners",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
